{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update.json\", \"summary\": \"Requested a delay sweep for the heartbeat term race, which currently rests on a single 0-2 ms comparison and whose own limitation says the shape against store latency is unmeasured. The harness reuses the same follower race and sweeps the maximum delay applied to the current-term write: 0, 250 us, 500 us, 1 ms and 2 ms, 200 attempts each, with a fresh store, transport and raft per case so a delay distribution cannot carry over. A local probe produced 0 inversions with no delay and then 88, 108, 104 and 98 at the four delay settings, which would mean the rate saturates almost immediately rather than growing with latency — the practical question the target's own divergence note raises when it accepts concurrent heartbeats to avoid inflating election timeouts for disk latency. Five comparisons assert that no delay setting may leave the node below the higher term, expecting the zero-delay case to hold and the rest to be violated, and each prerequisite pins the case's own maximum delay in microseconds so the curve is readable from the receipt. The submission validates with zero schema errors, the harness file exists, and it requests one execution.\"}"}}
